_:N18998895b48b46a0ac8b82f22b5ab1ae <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#first> <https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/RelationshipType/serializedInArtifact> .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/IsoAutomationLevel/conditionalAutomation> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Level 3 - Conditional automation. The system can propose strategies and then automatically execute the approved plan, with an external agent being ready to take over when necessary."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/ExpandedLicensing/standardAdditionTemplate> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Identifies the full text of a LicenseAddition, in SPDX templating format."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalRef> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "An External Reference points to a general resource outside the scope of the SPDX 3 content\nthat provides additional context, characteristics or related information about an Element."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/Bom> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "A Bill of Materials (BOM) is a container for a grouping of SPDX 3 content\ncharacterizing details about a product.\n\nThis could include details of the content and composition of the product,\nprovenance details of the product and/or\nits composition, licensing information, known quality or security issues, etc."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Security/catalogType> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#note> "A catalogType is a mandatory value and shall select one of the existing entries\nin the ExploitCatalogType vocabulary."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ProfileIdentifierType/service> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The element follows the Service profile specification."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/SupplyChain/UseProcess> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "UseProcess"@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/ExternalIdentifierType/isbn> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "International Standard Book Number (ISBN) <https://www.isbn-international.org/content/isbn-users-manual/29> is a unique numeric identifier for monographic publications standardized by ISO 2108 <https://www.iso.org/standard/65483.html>. It consists of either 10 digits (for assignments prior to January 1, 2007) or 13 digits. A 13-digit ISBN is composed of five parts: a GS1 prefix, a registration group, a registrant, a publication element, and a check digit. While elements may be divided by spaces or hyphens for human readability, these separators shall be omitted when the identifier is stored electronically (e.g., 9780198836063)."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Build/buildId> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "A buildId is a locally unique identifier used by a builder to identify a unique\ninstance of a build produced by it."@en .
<https://spdx.org/rdf/3.1/terms/Core/RelationshipType/coordinatedBy> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "The from Vulnerability is coordinatedBy the to Agent(s) (vendor, researcher, or consumer agent)."@en .
